@startuml possession-flow
' ⚠ THIS IS THE OVERVIEW — the whole possession on ONE SCREEN, and the only
' place the second-chance LOOP is visible as a loop. It is deliberately
' incomplete: every box here has a detail diagram that owns its branches.
'
' ⚠ WHERE TO ADD A BRANCH:
'   a new fork INSIDE a resolver  -> that resolver's own .puml (see the map below)
'   a new RESOLVER, or a new way the offense RETAINS -> here AND there
' A branch drawn in both places is a drift bug: this file owns the ORDER of the
' resolvers and the retention question; each detail file owns what happens inside.
'
' ⚠ THIS DIAGRAM TELLS THE STORY OF THE LOGIC. Notes say what the flow DOES;
' they do not argue why it was decided that way. The maths, the mechanics and
' every pass's history live in docs/possession-flow-model.md.
'
' ⚠ RENDERING — render the whole set with:
'   plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng docs/possession-flow*.puml
' Every diagram is now under PlantUML's 4096px default, so the flag is
' insurance rather than load-bearing (it was NOT, at 13,800px).
' ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out, so a green check does NOT prove the PNG is
' whole — and it does not catch deprecated syntax that RENDERS AS A WARNING
' BOX inside the image. Look at the PNG.
' ⚠ THE REAL CEILING IS THE SCREEN, ~2,000px — not 16,384. A diagram stops
' being readable long before PlantUML stops drawing it. This one especially.
' ⚠ `!include` does NOT help with that ceiling: an included fragment renders to
' the same height as inlining it. These are standalone diagrams on purpose.
title Possession Resolution — OVERVIEW\n//the whole possession; each resolver has its own diagram//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityFontSize 13
skinparam NoteFontSize 11

start

:**RotationState** — subs, fatigue, technical foul
//runs BETWEEN possessions, OUTSIDE the loop//
//→ possession-flow-rotation.puml//;

repeat
:**ShotSelector** — pick shooter, pick shot type
//the putback lives here: the rebounder's weight is boosted//
//→ possession-flow-shot-selection.puml//;

if (**TurnoverResolver** — turnover?\n//→ possession-flow-turnover.puml//) then (yes)
  :TURNOVER — one of nine causes
  //a charge also emits a FOUL — two events, one occurrence//;
  :**possession over**;
  stop
endif

if (**FoulResolver** — foul on the shot?\n//→ possession-flow-foul.puml//) then (yes)
  :FOUL + free throws
  //SHOOTING · NON_SHOOTING · FLAGRANT — one foul, three labels//;
  if (retains?\n//flagrant, or a missed LIVE last FT//) then (no)
    :**possession over**;
    stop
  else (yes — **RETAIN**)
  endif
endif

partition "**ShotResolver** — //→ possession-flow-shot.puml//" {
  if (made / blocked / missed?) then (MADE)
    :SHOT — MADE  (+ assist, + and-1)
    //an and-1's missed live FT can RETAIN//;
    :**possession over**;
    stop
  else if (BLOCKED) then
    :SHOT — BLOCKED  + a rebound credit
    //in-bounds recovery by the offense RETAINS//;
  else (MISSED)
  endif
}

if (**Rebounding foul**?\n//→ possession-flow-rebound.puml//) then (yes)
  :FOUL — REBOUNDING
  //defensive → offense RETAINS; offensive → ball flips//;
endif

:**MissedShotResolver** — the board, or out of bounds
//OFFENSIVE board or OOB-offense → RETAIN//
//→ possession-flow-rebound.puml//;

repeat while (**did the offense RETAIN?**\n//and retentions < MAX_OFFENSIVE_RETENTIONS_PER_POSSESSION//) is (yes — **second chance**) not (no)

:**possession over**;
note right
  ⚠ **SIX paths re-enter this loop**: the offensive rebound ·
  the block recovery · OOB-offense · the rebounding foul ·
  the flagrant retention · the missed LAST free throw.
   **ALL count against the ONE cap.**
  ⚠ **A SEVENTH is the signal to restructure this loop.**
  ⚠ Do NOT change the cap (3 → 5 is a parked idea needing its
  own recalibration pass — gametime-hey).
end note
stop

legend bottom left
  THIS IS THE OVERVIEW — it owns the ORDER of the resolvers and
  the retention question. Each resolver's branches live in its own
  diagram, and that file owns them:

  possession-flow-rotation.puml        subs · fatigue · the technical
  possession-flow-shot-selection.puml  who shoots · what shot · the putback
  possession-flow-turnover.puml        the gate · nine causes · the charge
  possession-flow-foul.puml            one foul, three labels · FTs · live board
  possession-flow-shot.puml            make/miss/block · recovery · assist · and-1
  possession-flow-rebound.puml         the rebounding foul · the four-way board

  ⚠ A fork INSIDE a resolver goes in that resolver's file. A new
  resolver, or a NEW WAY THE OFFENSE RETAINS, goes here too.

  The maths and every pass's history: possession-flow-model.md
  The event vocabulary:               game-events.md
endlegend

@enduml
